  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given below are two statements:</p><p><strong>Statement I :</strong>The average momentum of a molecule in a sample of an ideal gas depends on temperature.</p><p><strong>Statement II :</strong> The rms speed of oxygen molecules in a gas is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>. If the temperature is doubled and the oxygen molecules dissociate into oxygen atoms, the rms speed will become <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>v</mi></math>.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "3DoY0",
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "sGL1j",
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "FYCCG",
      "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "rm925",
      "text": "Statement I is false but Statement II is true",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Momentum is a vector quantity and average momentum of molecules of a sample is zero due to random motion.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>avg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>RMS speed of a molecule is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>rms</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi>M</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p>Now the temperature is doubled&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>new</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></math>&nbsp;and due to dissociation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>new</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub><mi>v</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac></msqrt><msqrt><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>M</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>v</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
